-- Tests of `types.tc_occurrence`'s own API: the evidence ids and cells a module mints
-- (`freshEvId`, `mintMethodCellRaw`, the site readers and `cellStoreMisses`, and the sites
-- the mark pass mints through `markGroupClauses`), the structural registries read off
-- interface declarations
-- (`argDispatchIndices`, `argDispatchIndicesById`, `methodConstraintNames`,
-- `constrainedSigNames`), the operator method tables and the goals an operator occurrence
-- records (`recordBinopGoals`, `recordUnopSite`, `recordIfaceObligation`,
-- `recordNegatedLitRange`), literal inference (`inferNumLit`), the method-occurrence
-- obligation (`mkMethodOccObl`), the obligations a standalone shadow's scheme re-records
-- (reached through `standaloneOccurrence`, which calls `recordShadowStandaloneObls`),
-- variable and standalone instantiation
-- (`instantiateVarTrackedId`, `standaloneSchemeFor`), the clause map of the mark pass
-- (`mapGroupClauses`, `markDictNames`), the write-back of marked clauses
-- (`rebuildGroupDecls`) and the ordinary-return probes
-- (`methodReturnResolutionMutationProbe`, `methodReturnTemplatePresenceProbe`).  Each test
-- builds the module record, environment and graph it reads; none reaches the inference
-- recursion.  `typecheck_test` also drives `cellGoalInnerAliasing`, which reads the goals of
-- a whole check, and the mark pass over a real program.

